#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:1
msgid "opt - LLVM optimizer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:8
msgid "{program}`opt` \\[*options*\\] \\[*filename*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:12
msgid ""
"The {program}`opt` command is the modular LLVM optimizer and analyzer. It "
"takes LLVM source files as input, runs the specified optimizations or "
"analyses on it, and then outputs the optimized file. The optimizations "
"available via {program}`opt` depend upon what libraries were linked into it "
"as well as any additional libraries that have been loaded with the {option}`-"
"load` option. Use the {option}`-help` option to determine what optimizations "
"you can use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:19
msgid ""
"If `filename` is omitted from the command line or is \"`-`\", {program}`opt` "
"reads its input from standard input. Inputs can be in either the LLVM "
"assembly language format (`.ll`) or the LLVM bitcode format (`.bc`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:23
msgid ""
"If an output filename is not specified with the {option}`-o` option, "
"{program}`opt` writes its output to the standard output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:26
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:29
msgid ""
"Enable binary output on terminals. Normally, {program}`opt` will refuse to "
"write raw bitcode output if the output stream is a terminal. With this "
"option, {program}`opt` will write raw bitcode regardless of the output "
"device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:35
msgid "Print a summary of command line options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:39
msgid "Specify the output filename."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:43
msgid "Write output in LLVM intermediate language (instead of bitcode)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:47
msgid ""
"A textual (comma-separated) description of the pass pipeline, e.g., `-"
"passes=\"sroa,instcombine\"`. See [invoking opt](../NewPassManager."
"md#invoking-opt) for more details on the pass pipeline syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:54
msgid ""
"Override the target triple specified in the input file with the specified "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:59
msgid ""
"Specify a specific chip microarchitecture in the current architecture to "
"tune code for. By default this is inferred from the target triple and "
"autodetected to the current architecture. For a list of available tuning "
"CPUs, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:70
msgid ""
"This option causes opt to strip debug information from the module before "
"applying other optimizations. It is essentially the same as `-strip` but it "
"ensures that stripping of debug information is done first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:76
msgid ""
"This option causes opt to add a verify pass after every pass otherwise "
"specified on the command line (including `-verify`). This is useful for "
"cases where it is suspected that a pass is creating an invalid module but it "
"is not clear which pass is doing it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:83
msgid "Print statistics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:87
msgid ""
"Save LLVM statistics to a file in the current directory ({option}`--save-"
"stats`/\"--save-stats=cwd\") or the directory of the output file (\"--save-"
"stats=obj\") in JSON format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:93
msgid ""
"Record the amount of time needed for each pass and print it to standard "
"error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:98
msgid ""
"If this is a debug build, this option will enable debug printouts from "
"passes which use the `LLVM_DEBUG()` macro. See {ref}`the LDBG and "
"LLVM_DEBUG() macros and -debug option <debug>` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:105
msgid ""
"Load the dynamic object `plugin`. This object should register new "
"optimization or analysis passes. Once loaded, the object will add new "
"command line options to enable various optimizations or analyses. To see the "
"new complete list of optimizations, use the {option}`-help` and {option}`-"
"load` options together. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:117
msgid "Print all available passes and exit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:120
msgid "EXIT STATUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/opt.md:122
msgid ""
"If {program}`opt` succeeds, it will exit with 0. Otherwise, if an error "
"occurs, it will exit with a non-zero value."
msgstr ""
